{"context": "published", "host": "www.josephsmithpapers.org", "showHeader": true, "footerStyle": "mini", "statusCode": 200, "uri": "letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830", "page": "6", "is404": false, "gallery": [{"image": "/52/52_ppallen_196_thumb.jpg", "page": "1", "label": "196", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/1"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_197_thumb.jpg", "page": "2", "label": "197", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/2"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_198_thumb.jpg", "page": "3", "label": "198", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/3"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_199_thumb.jpg", "page": "4", "label": "199", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/4"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_200_thumb.jpg", "page": "5", "label": "200", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/5"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_201_thumb.jpg", "page": "6", "label": "201", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/6"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_202_thumb.jpg", "page": "7", "label": "202", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/7"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_203_thumb.jpg", "page": "8", "label": "203", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/8"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_204_thumb.jpg", "page": "9", "label": "204", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/9"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_205_thumb.jpg", "page": "10", "label": "205", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/10"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_206_thumb.jpg", "page": "11", "label": "206", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/11"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_207_thumb.jpg", "page": "12", "label": "207", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/12"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_208_thumb.jpg", "page": "13", "label": "208", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/13"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_209_thumb.jpg", "page": "14", "label": "209", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/14"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_210_thumb.jpg", "page": "15", "label": "210", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/15"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_211_thumb.jpg", "page": "16", "label": "211", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/16"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD1", "documentSeriesTitle": "Letter to the Church in Colesville, 2 December 1830", "editorialPageNumber": "201", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/26086/26086-0006.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> and many have been buried under the ruins.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16412690698636466042\"><a href=\"#16412690698636466042\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans8\"><span id=\"documenttrans8\">8</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">In August 1830, Kingston, Jamaica, suffered a “tremendous hurricane” that caused “great injury” to ships and buildings and ruined the coffee and pimento crops. (“Hurricane,” <span class=\"title\">Rochester [NY] Republican,</span> 28 Sept. 1830, [1]; “Hurricane in the West Indies,” <span class=\"title\">New-York Spectator,</span> 23 Oct. 1830, 4.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\"><span class=\"title\">Rochester Republican.</span> Rochester, NY. 1829–1838.</p><p id=\"source-note2\"><span class=\"title\">New-York Spectator.</span> New York City. 1804–1867.</p></div></div></div></aside> In Columbia, South America, they are at war<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11920813216600623546\"><a href=\"#11920813216600623546\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans9\"><span id=\"documenttrans9\">9</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Late in 1830, Colombia was reportedly “sunk in the horrors of civil war” and in “a state of anarchy.” (“Colombia,” <span class=\"title\">Rochester [NY] Republican,</span> 9 Nov. 1830, [2]; see also “Colombia,” <span class=\"title\">Rochester [NY] Republican,</span> 5 Oct. 1830, [1].)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\"><span class=\"title\">Rochester Republican.</span> Rochester, NY. 1829–1838.</p></div></div></div></aside> and peace is taken from the earth in part. and it will soon be in whole,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9232595534291042423\"><a href=\"#9232595534291042423\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans10\"><span id=\"documenttrans10\">10</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Revelation 6:4.</p><hr></div></div></aside> yea destructions are at our doors, and they soon will be in the houses of the wicked, and they that know not God. Yea lift up your heads and rejoice for your redemption draweth nigh.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17515102457008098417\"><a href=\"#17515102457008098417\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans11\"><span id=\"documenttrans11\">11</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Luke 21:28. The same affirmation appeared in a revelation dictated a few days later. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-7-december-1830-dc-35\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-7-december-1830-dc-35\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 7 December 1830 [D&amp;C\n35]\">Revelation, 7 Dec. 1830</a> [D&amp;C 35:26].)</p><hr></div></div></aside> We are the most favored people that ever have been from the foundation of the world, if we remain faith [p. 201]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> and many have been buried <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>under the ruins.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14346862634812568216\"><a href=\"#14346862634812568216\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans8\"><span id=\"documenttrans8\">8</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">In August 1830, Kingston, Jamaica, suffered a “tremendous hurricane” that caused “great injury” to ships and buildings and ruined the coffee and pimento crops. (“Hurricane,” <span class=\"title\">Rochester [NY] Republican,</span> 28 Sept. 1830, [1]; “Hurricane in the West Indies,” <span class=\"title\">New-York Spectator,</span> 23 Oct. 1830, 4.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\"><span class=\"title\">Rochester Republican.</span> Rochester, NY. 1829–1838.</p><p id=\"source-note2\"><span class=\"title\">New-York Spectator.</span> New York City. 1804–1867.</p></div></div></div></aside> In Columbia, <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>South America, they are at <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>war<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16334708307069091167\"><a href=\"#16334708307069091167\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans9\"><span id=\"documenttrans9\">9</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Late in 1830, Colombia was reportedly “sunk in the horrors of civil war” and in “a state of anarchy.” (“Colombia,” <span class=\"title\">Rochester [NY] Republican,</span> 9 Nov. 1830, [2]; see also “Colombia,” <span class=\"title\">Rochester [NY] Republican,</span> 5 Oct. 1830, [1].)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\"><span class=\"title\">Rochester Republican.</span> Rochester, NY. 1829–1838.</p></div></div></div></aside> and peace is taken from <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the earth in part. and it will <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>soon be in whole,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9269960869940892528\"><a href=\"#9269960869940892528\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans10\"><span id=\"documenttrans10\">10</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Revelation 6:4.</p><hr></div></div></aside> yea des<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>tructions are at our doors, <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and they soon will be in <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the houses of the wicked, and <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>they that know not God. Yea <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>lift up your heads and rejoice <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>for your redemption draweth <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>nigh.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4858201898077829609\"><a href=\"#4858201898077829609\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans11\"><span id=\"documenttrans11\">11</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Luke 21:28. The same affirmation appeared in a revelation dictated a few days later. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-7-december-1830-dc-35\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-7-december-1830-dc-35\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 7 December 1830 [D&amp;C\n35]\">Revelation, 7 Dec. 1830</a> [D&amp;C 35:26].)</p><hr></div></div></aside> We are the most favored <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>people that ever have been <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>from the foundation of the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>world, if we remain faith [p. 201]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [], "images": {"smallImageUrl": "/52/52_ppallen_201_thumb.jpg", "mediumImageUrl": "/52/52_ppallen_201_med.jpg", "largeImageUrl": "/52/52_ppallen_201.jpg", "downloadImageUrl": "/52/52_ppallen_201_download.jpg"}, "imageCredit": "", "facsimile": "", "dzUrlXml": "/52/52_ppallen_201.xml", "classification": "Documents", "publishedStatus": "FinalContent", "accessionNumber": "52", "requestedPageNumber": "6", "numberOfPages": "16", "editorialTitle": "Letter to the Church in Colesville, 2 December 1830", "cleanEditorialTitle": "Letter to the Church in Colesville, 2 December 1830", "date": "December 2, 1830", "handwriting": "Handwriting", "footnotes": [{"id": "14346862634812568216", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">In Augu